## Why This Is Asked

Assesses planning, risk management, data integrity, and cross-team governance for a major migration; tests ability to define milestones, ownership, and metrics beyond high-level talk.

## Key Concepts

- Migration strategy and data integrity checks
- Downtime avoidance and phased rollout (canaries, dual-write)
- Rollback criteria, SLAs, and incident readiness
- Cross-team governance and staffing plans
- Metrics dashboards and validation artifacts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Basic idempotent migration hook (illustrative)
async function migrateBatch(batch) {
  for (const record of batch) {
    try {
      await writeToNewPlatform(record);
      await markAsMigrated(record.id);
    } catch (error) {
      await logMigrationError(record.id, error);
      // Continue processing other records
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This asks for a concrete governance approach to align many teams around data contracts, versioning, and regulatory constraints, a frequent real-world pain point in fintech.

## Key Concepts
- Contract driven development
- Data contracts and API versioning
- Cross team governance and automation
- Compliance and incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal contract validation skeleton
function validateContract(data, contract) {
  for (const field of contract.requiredFields) {
    if (data[field] === undefined) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure success and roll out across more teams?
- What are risks and mitigations for contract churn and migration?

## Interview Context
This question evaluates your ability to drive technical change without formal authority—a critical competency for senior engineers and engineering managers who must lead through influence rather than position power.

## Key Concepts
- **Strategic Stakeholder Mapping**: Using RACI (Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed) matrices to systematically identify decision-makers, influencers, and blockers across the organization
- **Data-Driven Influence**: Leveraging quantitative evidence including A/B testing results, performance metrics, and business impact data to build compelling technical arguments
- **Technical Credibility Building**: Establishing authority through comprehensive documentation, working prototypes, and consistent delivery of high-quality technical solutions

